.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_COLLECTION_REDUCE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_collection_reduce ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_reduce_named ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_count ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_distinct ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_threshold ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_threshold_named ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_count_total ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_distinct_total ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_threshold_total ,
.Nm dtfl_reduce_emit_pair
.Nd group a collection by key and reduce the values per key
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/reduce.h
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_reduce_emit_pair "dtfl_reduce_emit *e" "const void *val" "size_t vlen" "const void *diff"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_type *key_type" "const dtfl_type *val_type" "const dtfl_type *out_val" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_reduce_fn logic" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce_named "dtfl_collection *c" "const char *name" "const dtfl_type *key_type" "const dtfl_type *val_type" "const dtfl_type *out_val" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_reduce_fn logic" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_count "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_distinct "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_threshold "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_threshold_fn thresh" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_threshold_named "dtfl_collection *c" "const char *name" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_threshold_fn thresh" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_count_total "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_distinct_total "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_threshold_total "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_threshold_fn thresh" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The reduce family groups a collection by key and applies a user reduction
to the multiset of values accumulated under each key.
These operators are incremental: when a key's accumulated input changes at a
new logical time, the operator retracts the output it produced before and
asserts the new output, so the collection each defines is the exact function
of its input at every time.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce_named
group
.Fa c ,
whose records are a key followed by a value
.Pq key || val ,
split by
.Fa key_type ,
with the value side described by
.Fa val_type .
For each key the
.Fa logic
callback receives the key and the accumulated input multiset, an array of
.Fa n
value and difference pairs presented in the order of
.Fa val_type ,
and emits output value and difference pairs through the
.Vt dtfl_reduce_emit
handle with
.Fn dtfl_reduce_emit_pair .
Each emitted value is of
.Fa out_val
and each difference is of
.Fa out_diff ,
which must be an Abelian class.
The result is a collection of records
.Pq key || out_val
with differences of
.Fa out_diff .
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce
names the operator
.Dq Reduce ;
.Fn dtfl_collection_reduce_named
takes an explicit
.Fa name .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_count
counts the occurrences of each key.
The whole record of
.Fa c
is the key.
For each key it emits the record
.Pq key || count ,
where the count is the summed input difference rendered as a value of the
input difference class, with an output difference of one of
.Fa out_diff ,
which must be Abelian and have a one
.Pq for example Fn dtfl_diff_i64 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_distinct
reduces the collection to one occurrence of each key whose accumulated
difference is non-zero, with a difference of one of
.Fa out_diff .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_threshold
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_threshold_named
transform the multiplicity of each key.
The
.Fa thresh
callback maps a key's accumulated input difference to an output difference of
.Fa out_diff
by writing it through
.Fa out
and returning true, or returns false to emit nothing.
The operator emits the change in that output across times, so the predicate
need not be incremental.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_count_total ,
.Fn dtfl_collection_distinct_total
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_threshold_total
are optimizations of count, distinct and threshold for a totally ordered
time
.Pq Fn dtfl_time_is_total .
They read the input trace before the current batch to recover each key's
accumulated difference and emit the change directly, without the general
reduce engine; they panic if the time class is not totally ordered.
Their results match the general operators.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each function returns a new
.Vt dtfl_collection
handle the caller frees with
.Fn dtfl_collection_free .
Allocation failure is reported through the panic hook, as elsewhere in the
library.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_arrange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_new 3
.Sh STANDARDS
These operators port differential dataflow's
.Fn reduce ,
.Fn count ,
.Fn distinct
and
.Fn threshold
collection methods from the pinned upstream
.Pq differential-dataflow-v0.25.1 .
